BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newburyport Art presents Fleeting Moments: Photography by Geordie 
 Vining
DTSTART:20260909T110000
DTEND:20260920T170000
DTSTAMP:20260829T140301Z
UID:0012e0eb2e5f7ecfba0a78cb7e496b@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA) is excited to announce Fleeting Moments:
  Spontaneous Photography by Featured Artist Geordie Vining. Geordie Vining
  has worked as the Senior Project Manager for the Newburyport Planning Off
 ice for 25 years. Among many projects\, Geordie managed the creation of th
 e Clipper City Rail Trail from concept to completion. He also managed desi
 gn and construction of the Senior Community Center\, the John F. Cutter Jr
 . Fire Station\, and the Harbormaster Visiting Boater Facility\, as well a
 s co-founded the award-winning Newburyport Black History Initiative. Outsi
 de of his work for the Newburyport Planning Office\, Geordie is a photogra
 pher who focuses on capturing a range of unplanned photographs of unique 
 “fleeting moments.” Vining writes\, “Such pictures can speak to the 
 human condition\, tell a story\, and hold on to a glimpse of fleeting beau
 ty.” His photographs are nearly all spontaneous and unplanned\, ranging 
 from close-ups to wide shots\, and from vibrant colors to classic black-an
 d-white. The images are of people\; townscapes and cityscapes\; landscapes
 \; the natural world\; and abstract or ambiguous scenes. Many of the pictu
 res are of his home in New England\, but also from other parts of the Unit
 ed States\, as well as countries like Norway\, Portugal\, Canada\, France
 \, England\, Italy\, Croatia\, Japan\, and a growing list of others. Fleet
 ing moments transform into art. Join us for a free opening reception on We
 dnesday\, September 2\, 5:00pm-7:00pm. Fleeting Moments: Spontaneous Photo
 graphy is partially supported by the Newburyport Cultural Council\, West N
 ewbury Cultural Council\, and Mass Cultural Council. The galleries are fre
 e and open to the public Wednesday through Sunday from 11:00am–5:00pm. N
 ewburyport Art is closed on Mondays and Tuesdays. The ground-floor Hills G
 allery has an accessible entrance. More information\, as well as an online
  gallery is available at newburyportart.org. Founded in 1948\, Newburyport
  Art is a 501(c)(3) non-profit organization dedicated to promoting and exh
 ibiting members’ work and to providing art education and access to the v
 isual arts for the entire community.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent pa
 ge: https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-fleeting-mome
 nts-photography-by-geordie-vining/2026-09-09/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-fleeting-mome
 nts-photography-by-geordie-vining/2026-09-09/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newburyport Art presents May Exhibitions at 65 Water Street
DTSTART:20260909T110000
DTEND:20260909T170000
DTSTAMP:20260829T140301Z
UID:0d47de3aca7e3e16b597fb9aa52f68@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA) presents three new shows opening in the 
 month of May! Soft Structures is a group exhibition that explores fibers a
 nd fibrous material as process and metaphor. This exhibit features over 80
  artworks in a variety of media including drawing\, painting\, sculpture\,
  weaving\, embroidery\, quilting\, collage\, mixed media and more. This ex
 hibit is on view in the first-floor Sargent Gallery and second-floor Harts
 on Gallery. FOLIA is a collaborative exhibition featuring works by Amesbur
 y artists Amy Vander Els & Heather Karp. This exhibit explores the quiet b
 eauty and joyful rhythm of leaves and the symbolic meaning behind many tha
 t speaks of perseverance\, resilience and hope. Thirty-six artworks are di
 splayed amongst spring greenery in the first-floor Hills Gallery. Amy and 
 Heather will give a free artist talk on Thursday\, May 21st from 6:00-7:00
 pm\, concluding with Q&A. The 11th Annual Outdoor Sculpture Garden Exhibit
 ion debuted on May 1st\, and will remain on view year-round until April 20
 27. At nearly 3\,000 square feet\, the Range Lights Sculpture Garden resid
 es behind the historic NAA and is seen and visited by hundreds of people e
 very week. This year’s exhibition features 16 pieces by 10 local and reg
 ional artists. The participating artists include\; Jeffrey Briggs\, Lindle
 y Briggs\, Sarah Burns and Mike Platt\, Alexis Guieb-Alimbuyuguen\, Andrew
  Henschel\, Mae Kenny\, Evan Ralph\, Michael Updike and Raynor Warner. A r
 eception for FOLIA and Soft Structures will be held on Saturday\, May 2nd 
 from 4-6pm\, with the 11th Annual Sculpture Exhibit reception beginning at
  3:00pm\, including a Best in Show award at 3:30pm. The receptions are fre
 e and open to the public\, and visitors participating in the May 2nd Newbu
 ryport Artwalk are encouraged to stop by. New Hours: Wednesday through Sun
 day from 11:00am–5:00pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More inform
 ation\, as well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.org. F
 ounded in 1948\, Newburyport Art\, a 501(c)(3) non-profit\, is dedicated t
 o promoting and exhibiting members’ work and to providing art education 
 and access to the visual arts for the entire community. The gallery and ev
 ents are free and open to the public.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent p
 age: https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibiti
 ons-at-65-water-street/2026-09-09/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibitio
 ns-at-65-water-street/2026-09-09/
END:VEVENT
