BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CAM Talk: Cape Ann Museum – Then\, Now\, and Tomorrow
DTSTART:20260913T140000
DTEND:20260913T153000
DTSTAMP:20260829T140301Z
UID:fdced1906b089c67955773e9dc273c@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join the Bayliss Society at the Cape Ann Museum on September 1
 3 for the closing program of this year’s Jonathan Bayliss Society annual
  conference\, “Gloucester’s Acropolis: Defining the City Then and Now.
 ” This final session features a series of short talks exploring the role
  and influence of Cape Ann Museum in the community life of Gloucester thro
 ughout its existence\, with a glimpse toward an exciting future as well. S
 peakers are CAM’s Director Oliver Barker\, Chief Curator Martha Oaks\, a
 nd former Museum volunteer Deanie Hancock French. Deanie’s father\, the 
 major American sculptor Walker Hancock\, was involved for many years in th
 e development of what was then called the Cape Ann Historical Association.
  About the Conference Novelist Jonathan Bayliss (1926–2009) coined the t
 erm Acropolis to describe the cluster of civic institutions rising above G
 loucester Harbor—City Hall\, Sawyer Free Library\, the Museum\, and neig
 hboring landmarks. This year’s conference brings that idea to life throu
 gh talks\, walks\, and readings from September 11–13\, exploring how thi
 s hillside cultural district has shaped Gloucester from the 19th century t
 o today. The conference is organized by the Jonathan Bayliss Society in co
 llaboration with Cape Ann Museum\, Gloucester Writers Center\, and Sawyer 
 Free Library\, with support from the Gloucester Cultural Council\, Mass Cu
 ltural Council\, and the Bruce Cove Foundation. More information is availa
 ble at www.jonathanbayliss.org/acropolis.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEve
 nt page: https://northofboston.org/event/cam-talk-cape-ann-museum-then-now
 -and-tomorrow/
LOCATION:Cape Ann Museum\, 27 Pleasant Street\, Gloucester\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/cam-talk-cape-ann-museum-then-now-and-
 tomorrow/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Closing Night: On the Ocean’s Edge
DTSTART:20260913T170000
DTEND:20260913T183000
DTSTAMP:20260829T140301Z
UID:60c3b9be3f708d8a329f4999023274@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Maeve Gilchrist | Seamus Egan | David Coffin | Trio Oko | Nual
 a Kennedy | The Rockport Celtic Festival House Band In this jam packed eve
 ning we bring together some of the most cutting edge sounds from the Celti
 c World as well as local Cape Ann hero\, David Coffin and the innovative n
 ew Harp Trio\, Trio Oko. In tonight’s performance we present a World Pre
 mier by the Irish singer and flautist\, Nuala Kennedy. A four part suite o
 f music inspired by the fire festivals which mark the seasons of the tradi
 tional Celtic Year: Samhain (Winter)\, Imbolc (Spring)\, Bealtaine (Summer
 ) and Lunasa (Autumn). With poetry woven throughout\, this world premier w
 ill be performed by Nuala with the incredible House band (Logan Coale\, Ma
 eve Gilchrist\, Alan Murray and more) In the first act of the show\, Irish
  Music Legend\, Seamus Egan and Artistic Director Maeve Gilchrist join for
 ces with strings to perform tunes from their new album ‘Into the Ice’
 \, a sonic retelling of the famous Shackleton expedition\, through the len
 s of traditional Irish Music\, electronics and prose. Prepare to be transp
 orted! In addition we have two more of Vivaldi’s seasons to round off th
 e year\, sing-along shanties with the inimitable David Coffin and all type
 s of one-off collaborations including a harp duet and lush string arrangem
 ents of traditional Celtic tunes!\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page:
  https://northofboston.org/event/closing-night-on-the-oceans-edge/
LOCATION:Shalin Liu Performance Center\, 37 Main Street\, Rockport\, MA\, 
 01966
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/closing-night-on-the-oceans-edge/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Daily Guided & Self-Guided Tour of Hammond Castle Museum
DTSTART:20260913T090000
DTEND:20260913T153000
DTSTAMP:20260829T140301Z
UID:eb9b43e76481de0869f50a46402499@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step inside the breathtaking home of one of the most prolific 
 inventors of the 20th century\, John Hays Hammond\, Jr. Hammond Castle Mus
 eum is a dynamic STEAM museum\,*blending its historical significance as bo
 th **a historic house museum and a lapidarium. Inside\, you’ll not only 
 discover ancient\, medieval\, and Renaissance architectural elements and a
 rtifacts—including stone archways\, sarcophagi\, grave markers\, and an 
 extraordinary collection of stone and marble works—but you’ll also fin
 d a vibrant museum offering fresh educational and cultural arts programmin
 g. Visitors can explore items from the archival collection that have not b
 een publicly seen in generations\, along with newly curated content and th
 e most up-to-date information on the provenance of many pieces in our coll
 ection. New this season\, the Museum features four temporary exhibits that
  explore John Hays Hammond Jr. as both an individual and a scientific inno
 vator. In the Natalie Hays Hammond Temporary Exhibit Room\, Curatorial Dir
 ector John Leysath presents Spinning Platters with Hammond: Inside the Wor
 ld of Vinyl Records\, on display from April 29th through August 31st. Begi
 nning September 10th and running through the end of the 2025 season on Jan
 uary 4th\, Leysath will showcase” Hammond in Italy: The Love Affair Betw
 een the Hammonds & Italian Culture.”Additionally\, the Inventions Exhibi
 t Room will highlight Hammond’s groundbreaking Videotape Technology duri
 ng the spring and summer months\, followed by Hammond’s ahead-of-their-t
 ime Advertising Signs in the fall and early winter. Listed on the National
  Register of Historic Places\, and a repeated Reader’s Choice Best of No
 rth Shore winner by Northshore Magazine and a Trip Advisor Traveler’s Ch
 oice award recipient for the last three consecutive years\,** you can trus
 t that your visit will be an unforgettable experience. New This Season: Ne
 w Daily Hours and Flexible Arrival Times for Self-Guided Tours Open daily 
 from 9:00 am to 3:30 pm\, with the last entrance at 2:45 pm. The Museum\, 
 Museum Shop\, and grounds close at 3:30 pm. Experience Hammond Castle Muse
 um at your own pace with our new flexible arrival times for self-guided to
 urs. Your ticket grants you entry anytime within designated periods\, ensu
 ring you can arrive stress-free and enjoy your visit to the fullest. Morni
 ng Session: 9:00 am – 11:45 am / Afternoon Session: 11:45 am – 2:30 pm
  Self-guided tours allow you to explore at your own pace. We recommend pla
 nning for at least 60 minutes to experience the Museum’s fascinating gal
 leries\, grounds\, and temporary exhibits. **Accessibility Note: Please be
  aware that at nearly a century old\, the Hammond Castle Museum is not han
 dicapped accessible due to many difficult and winding stairs on the campus
  and within the Museum\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://no
 rthofboston.org/event/daily-guided-self-guided-tour-of-hammond-castle-muse
 um/2026-09-13/
LOCATION:Hammond Castle Museum\, 80 Hesperus Avenue\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01
 930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/daily-guided-self-guided-tour-of-hammo
 nd-castle-museum/2026-09-13/
END:VEVENT
