BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Open Studios: Fiona Sinéad Brehony\, GAR Environmental / Installa
 tion Artist
DTSTART:20260924T140000
DTEND:20260924T160000
DTSTAMP:20260829T140301Z
UID:e3b3ded10154f68e7ad1fafe094add@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join Fiona Sinéad Brehony\, the 2026 GAR Environmental / Inst
 allation Artist\, to see her work in progress at Ocean Alliance on Thursda
 y\, September 17 or Thursday\, September 24 from 2-4 pm. This residency of
 fers Brehony an opportunity to explore Gloucester Harbor through Richard W
 hite’s concept of the organic machine\, simultaneously a natural system 
 and human infrastructure\, yet also something so vast and distributed it e
 xceeds our ability to fully grasp it. She will engage in acts of listening
 \, watching and writing to see what emerges\, inviting participants in for
  gatherings where ideas can transform collectively. Working with Ocean All
 iance’s whale song archives\, she hopes to develop poetic work that expl
 ores ocean presence\, waters shared with whales\, where freshwater meets s
 alt and interaction shifts from intimate to incomprehensible.\n\nSources: 
 North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/open-studios-
 fiona-sinead-brehony-gar-environmental-installation-artist/2026-09-24/
LOCATION:Ocean Alliance\, 32 Horton Street\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01930-1836
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/open-studios-fiona-sinead-brehony-gar-
 environmental-installation-artist/2026-09-24/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spiritualism Tours by Candlelight at Hammond Castle Museum
DTSTART:20260924T180000
DTEND:20260924T210000
DTSTAMP:20260829T140301Z
UID:d28580221bbbc36d389c2022fa699a@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:From John Hays Hammond Jr.’s attempts to communicate with su
 pernatural entities using a Faraday Cage to Irene Fenton Hammond’s exten
 sive astrological writings under a mysterious pen name\, this 55-minute\, 
 fully-guided specialty tour sets the stage for a fun and informative seaso
 nal experience unlike any other. The dramatic\, Gothic-inspired architectu
 re of the Museum and the twilight atmosphere are enhanced by the light of 
 handheld electronic lanterns throughout your tour. New in 2026: Extended H
 ours and Midnight Tours For the first time\, Hammond Castle Museum is offe
 ring its popular Spiritualism Tours by Candlelight during extended late-ni
 ght hours–including a midnight tour–on October 22nd and 29th—a one-o
 f-a-kind experience for those celebrating the Halloween season on the Nort
 h Shore! Admission: July\, August\, & September: $27.50. October: $35. Mus
 eum Member savings apply. Please be mindful when processing your reservati
 on to select the correct reservation date and corresponding admission pric
 e.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/even
 t/spiritualism-tours-by-candlelight-at-hammond-castle-museum-2/2026-09-24/
LOCATION:Hammond Castle Museum\, 80 Hesperus Avenue\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01
 930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/spiritualism-tours-by-candlelight-at-h
 ammond-castle-museum-2/2026-09-24/
END:VEVENT
