BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Direct from NYC: A Night of Big Apple Comedy
DTSTART:20261017T200000
DTEND:20261017T214500
DTSTAMP:20260829T140301Z
UID:2d83d6c4fef9555cd8e74ecea9cf4a@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Get ready—New York City comedy is coming to the Larcom Theat
 re for one unforgettable night! Three hilarious comics are bringing the sh
 arp wit\, fast laughs\, and unmistakable energy of the Big Apple to the No
 rth Shore. Headliner Mark Riccadonna is a contributing writer for “Weeke
 nd Update” on NBC’s Saturday Night Live and the star of the Dry Bar Co
 medy special Domestic Nomad. His credits also include Live at Gotham on AX
 S TV and comedy tours around the world with the USO and Armed Forces Enter
 tainment. Featured comic Chris Larry has appeared in the Kenan Thompson Pr
 esents series and at the Savannah Comedy Review and Good Karma Comedy Fest
 ival. He is also a host and writer for PLUMP\, a New York City multimedia 
 entertainment company. Hosting the evening is Frank Vignola\, whose credit
 s include Comedy Central\, SiriusXM\, Montreal’s prestigious Just for La
 ughs Comedy Festival\, and Amazon Prime. From smart storytelling and relat
 able observations to quick wit and unexpected punchlines\, this powerhouse
  lineup is perfect for a night out with friends\, date night\, or anyone w
 ho could use a big laugh.​ Don’t miss an unforgettable night of NYC co
 medy!​ Duration: 90 minutes + intermission Age Recommendation: 18+ Thela
 rcom.org/bigapplecomedy\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://n
 orthofboston.org/event/direct-from-nyc-a-night-of-big-apple-comedy/
LOCATION:Larcom Theatre\, 13 Wallis Street\, Beverly\, MA\, 01915
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/direct-from-nyc-a-night-of-big-apple-c
 omedy/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Macbeth
DTSTART:20261017T130000
DTEND:20261017T150000
DTSTAMP:20260829T140301Z
UID:076cb727a5a615e5446de860ba218f@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Music by Giuseppe Verdi | Libretto by Francesco Maria Piave an
 d Andrea Maffei Two of opera’s most extraordinary artists return to The 
 Met: Live in HD for Verdi’s thrilling take on the immortal Shakespearean
  tale of the scheming couple determined to seize power at any cost. Barito
 ne Quinn Kelsey is the Scottish king haunted by the ghosts of his murderou
 s ascent to the throne\, opposite soprano Lise Davidsen as the power-mad L
 ady Macbeth\, whose ruinous ambition damns them both. Met Music Director Y
 annick Nézet-Séguin takes the podium for a penetrating production by Lou
 isa Proske. Rounding out the all-star cast are tenor Freddie De Tommaso as
  Macduff and bass-baritone Ryan Speedo Green as Banquo. Conductor: Yannick
  Nézet-Séguin Production: Louisa Proske Lady Macbeth: Lise Davidsen Set 
 Designer: Jon Bausor Macduff: Freddie De Tommaso Costume Designer: Montana
  Levi Blanco Macbeth: Quinn Kelsey Lighting Designer: Adam Silverman Banqu
 o: Ryan Speedo Green Choreographer: Jorrell Lawyer-Jefferson Action Direct
 or: Ran Arthur Braun C. Graham Berwind\, III Chorus Director: Tilman Micha
 el\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/even
 t/macbeth-2/
LOCATION:Shalin Liu Performance Center\, 37 Main Street\, Rockport\, MA\, 
 01966
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/macbeth-2/
END:VEVENT
