BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spiritualism Tours by Candlelight at Hammond Castle Museum
DTSTART:20261022T180000
DTEND:20261022T233000
DTSTAMP:20260829T140301Z
UID:2e9f7d2e543c627e35c5ef86671f21@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:From John Hays Hammond Jr.’s attempts to communicate with su
 pernatural entities using a Faraday Cage to Irene Fenton Hammond’s exten
 sive astrological writings under a mysterious pen name\, this 55-minute\, 
 fully-guided specialty tour sets the stage for a fun and informative seaso
 nal experience unlike any other. The dramatic\, Gothic-inspired architectu
 re of the Museum and the twilight atmosphere are enhanced by the light of 
 handheld electronic lanterns throughout your tour. New in 2026: Extended H
 ours and Midnight Tours For the first time\, Hammond Castle Museum is offe
 ring its popular Spiritualism Tours by Candlelight during extended late-ni
 ght hours–including a midnight tour–on October 22nd and 29th—a one-o
 f-a-kind experience for those celebrating the Halloween season on the Nort
 h Shore! Admission: July\, August\, & September: $27.50. October: $35. Mus
 eum Member savings apply. Please be mindful when processing your reservati
 on to select the correct reservation date and corresponding admission pric
 e.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/even
 t/spiritualism-tours-by-candlelight-at-hammond-castle-museum-3/2026-10-22/
LOCATION:Hammond Castle Museum\, 80 Hesperus Avenue\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01
 930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/spiritualism-tours-by-candlelight-at-h
 ammond-castle-museum-3/2026-10-22/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
